# Cine Lenses and Formats
#
# Motion-picture formats compared by gate size, diagonal, squeeze, and delivered ratio, with the arithmetic that turns a 4:3 gate and a 2x anamorphic into 2.66 before the crop to 2.39.

#>optics_cine_formats
#:layer #!pragmatics
#:domain #!optics
#:form #!comparison
#:level #!practitioner
#:review #!adversarial_checked
#:valence #!bone
#:era #!modern

^"emit"{
 ~#title: "Cine Lenses and Formats"
 ~#claim: "A 4:3 gate de-squeezed by a 2x anamorphic is about 2.66 wide, so 4:3 digital modes reach the 2.39 scope ratio only after cropping."
 ~#proof: "The American Cinematographer Manual for gates, frame counts, and T-stops; Belton for CinemaScope history; manufacturer figures as verify cells."
 ~#door: "Squeeze a photo by half and stretch it back, then read the format matrix row for your camera."
 ~#audience: "camera assistants, cinematographers, film students, and editors"
 continuity: "Cine Lenses and Formats | after cropping"
 cold_open: "An anamorphic lens squeezes a wide world onto a squarer gate, and the scope ratio appears only after cropping."
}

